Next.js serves this directory at the site root, and `frontend/Dockerfile`
copies it into the runtime image with `COPY --from=build /app/public ./public`.

The product has no static assets today -- the favicon is `src/app/icon.svg`,
which Next handles -- so the directory would otherwise be empty, and Git does
not track empty directories. That made the frontend image buildable only from
cache: a build from a fresh clone failed with

    failed to calculate checksum of ref ...: "/app/public": not found

which is a build that has been broken for as long as nobody tried it. Found by
building a release candidate from a clean clone.

This file exists so the directory does.
